OpenWings patch 0014: long commands marked #!bg run in the code runner

Upstream's bash prompt asks the model to start anything over about 20
seconds with a #!bg line, which launches a detached job. Detached jobs
need bubblewrap containment, which Docker does not allow, so in a Docker
install every such command failed with "containment unavailable", even
with the OpenWings code runner on.

  * src/tool_execution.py: with the runner enabled, a #!bg command skips
    the detached job path and goes through the normal bash path to the
    runner. wings/runner.py drops the marker line, gives the command the
    runner's full time limit (WINGS_RUNNER_MAX_TIMEOUT) and tells the
    model it ran in the foreground, so it does not wait for a follow-up.

Without the runner, upstream behaviour is unchanged.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

diff --git a/src/tool_execution.py b/src/tool_execution.py
index a410f40..2611ecb 100644
--- a/src/tool_execution.py
+++ b/src/tool_execution.py
@@ -2152,6 +2152,13 @@ async def _execute_tool_block_impl(
     # monitor re-invokes the agent with the full output when the job finishes.
     if tool == "bash" and session_id and (backend is None or isinstance(backend.resource, NativeBackendResource)):
         _is_bg, _bg_cmd = _split_bg_marker(content)
+        # Wings: detached jobs need bubblewrap containment, which Docker does
+        # not allow, so this path always failed. With the code runner on, the
+        # command runs there in the foreground instead (the marker is a bash
+        # comment), with the runner's full time limit; see wings/runner.py.
+        from wings import runner as _wings_runner
+        if _is_bg and _bg_cmd and _wings_runner.enabled():
+            _is_bg = False
         if _is_bg and _bg_cmd:
             from src import bg_jobs
             mark_dispatch()
